/-! # VII-08 (2/5): actual Kerr–Schild difference connection and acceleration transfer

Same chart, open `U`, raw `KSData b bi v k U`. With the **registered** `christoffel`:

* `Γ̄ = christoffel b bi` (background, non-constant in general), `Γ = christoffel g gi` for the
  Kerr–Schild pair `g = ksMetric b v k`, `gi = ksInverse bi v k`;
* `C = Γ − Γ̄` (`ksC`), `(∇̄_c k)^a = ∂_c k^a + Σ_l Γ̄^a_{cl} k^l` (`covD`, an explicit finite sum),
  `A = accel b bi k` (VII-07 actual acceleration), `a_d = Σ_j b_dj A^j`, `k(v) = Σ_c k^c ∂_c v`.

Proved on `U` from the raw data only (no geodesic, flatness, `v ≠ 0` or `k ≠ 0` hypothesis):

1. differentiated nullity / background metric compatibility: `Σ_a ℓ_a (∇̄_c k)^a = 0`;
2. lowered difference connection `Σ_i g_di C^i_{pq} = ½(∇̄_q h_{dp} + ∇̄_p h_{dq} − ∇̄_d h_{pq})`
   with `∇̄_c h_{pq}` (`nablaH`) written explicitly for `h = v ℓ ⊗ ℓ`;
3. `M^a_p = Σ_q C^a_{pq} k^q = ½[k(v) k^a ℓ_p + v A^a ℓ_p + v k^a a_p]`;
4. `Σ_{pq} C^a_{pq} k^p k^q = 0`, `Σ_a C^a_{aq} = 0` (trace of the **difference** connection);
5. `accel g gi k = accel b bi k`, hence actual pregeodesic / affine conditions are equivalent
   (same multiplier; non-affine parametrisation allowed).

All derivative facts are genuine (`pd_mul`, `pd_sum`, `pd_congr_of_eqOn` on the open `U`); the
nullity identity is differentiated only because it holds on the whole open `U`.
